import FormalConjectures.Arxiv.«2604.08040».Conjecture5_5

/-!
# `Arxiv.«2604.08040».cyc_alternatingGroup_five`

Upstream: `Arxiv.«2604.08040».cyc_alternatingGroup_five` (category test), `FormalConjectures/Arxiv/2604.08040/Conjecture5_5.lean` line 119.
Proof idea: every element of `A₅` has order `1`, `2`, `3` or `5` (checked by kernel `decide`),
so the cyclic subgroup generated by `g` has the explicit, computable carrier
`{g ^ k | k < 5}`. A subgroup is cyclic iff it is `zpowers g` for some `g`, and a subgroup is
